# Git commits and pushes

- Follow the commit message convention in `README.md` (`Type: Summary`).
- For work under `projects/`, use `Project(<folder-name>): Summary.` The folder name is the directory under `projects/` (e.g. `Project(project-management): Add prettier to the codebase.`). Do not use `Project: Summary` without the folder name, and do not use a second colon.
- Never add a `Co-authored-by:` trailer (including `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>`).
- Do not append any AI/tool attribution lines to commit messages.
- Keep messages as the user-approved text only.

## Timestamps (required)

GitHub shows **author date**, not committer date, and not push time. The user wants that stamp to be the real `git commit` time.

- New commits: do not set `GIT_AUTHOR_DATE`. Let Git use now for both author and committer.
- Never `export GIT_AUTHOR_DATE`, `GIT_AUTHOR_NAME`, `GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL`, or `GIT_COMMITTER_DATE` in a persistent shell. If `commit-tree` needs them, pass them as a **one-shot prefix on that command only**.
- After any rewrite, run `unset GIT_AUTHOR_DATE GIT_AUTHOR_NAME GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL GIT_COMMITTER_DATE`.
- When stripping a trailer from a commit just created, copy that commit's existing dates only if they are current. If author date is stale, set author date to the committer date (the real commit time).
- `git push` does not record a time on the commit. Do not try to set dates to push time.

## After every commit (required)

Cursor may inject `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` even when the agent did not write it.

1. Run `git log -1 --format=full` immediately after commit or amend.
2. If any `Co-authored-by:` (or other AI/tool trailer) is present, rewrite the HEAD message to the approved text only, then verify again.
3. Prefer `git commit --amend` when the amend rules allow it. If amend re-injects the trailer, recreate HEAD with the same tree via `git commit-tree` and `git reset --soft` (unpushed commits only). Pass author env as a one-shot prefix; never `export` it.
4. Do not finish the turn until `git log -1 --format=%B` has no `Co-authored-by:` line.

## Before every push (required)

- Do not push if HEAD (or any commit being pushed) contains `Co-authored-by:`.
- Strip it first, then push.
